                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2611.24789/2611.24789v1/opsd_wam.png",
                "caption": "Figure 2:Overview of HINT-WAM.Stage 0 (top left):the action expert is fine-tuned with flow matching on demonstrations, conditioned on the key/value cache of the frozen video expert, giving the student initialization.Stage A (top right):with the SFT model frozen, a hindsight encoder compresses the demonstration’s future observations into hindsight tokens, which the action expert reads through gated cross-attention adapters; only the encoder and adapters are trained.Stage B (bottom):the student integrates its own ODE without gradients, and its implied actions at selected denoising points are matched to a single sample from the frozen hindsight teacher with the energy score, together with a behavior-cloning anchor. Only the student is deployed.",
                "position": 427
            }
